# /sdd-compact

Purpose:
  Compress the SDD working context to essential tokens — persisting SDD
  state first, then delegating the actual context compaction to the AI
  agent's NATIVE /compact so the agent's own summarization is used
  instead of being fought or reimplemented (Phase 152).

Owns: commands/sdd-compact.sdd

Description:
  Compress current context to essential tokens only. Use after completing
  a task to minimize token usage before next operation. Delegates the
  compaction itself to the host agent's native /compact.

Usage:
  /sdd-compact
  /sdd-compact --keep-decisions
  /sdd-compact --keep-references

Options:
  --keep-decisions    Preserve decision records
  --keep-references   Preserve reference index

Behavior:
  1. Persist current task state (checkpoints [RT8]; token count)
  2. Summarize current task output to essential facts
  3. Keep decisions, references, and next actions per options
  4. Append the /sdd* prompt pair to prompts/history/prompt-pairs.jsonl ([R104])
  5. DELEGATE: instruct the agent to run its NATIVE /compact (Claude Code,
     Kilo /compact) — never reimplement or shadow native context commands
  6. Persist compressed state; report token savings

Output:
  [tokens: before=X, after=Y, saved=Z%]
  [state: compacted]
  [native: /compact delegated]

Navigation:
  MemoryModel: @../runtime/memory-model.sdd
  MemoryConsolidation: @../runtime/memory-consolidation.sdd
  CleanCommand: @sdd-clean.sdd

State: +
   (Phase 152: header fixed to /sdd-compact; behavior now persists SDD
   state then delegates compaction to the host agent's native /compact)
